      "description": "Watch Santos vs Chapecoense AF highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The Vila Belmiro set the stage for a high-stakes Serie A encounter on July 26, 2026 , as Santos FC hosted Chapecoense AF . Both teams arrived with a clear tactical plan, creating an atmosphere of intense competition from the opening whistle in this crucial football match . Neymar Sets the Tone in the First Half Santos controlled much of the early proceedings, utilizing the creativity of their midfield to stretch the Chapecoense defense. The breakthrough came in the 36th minute when Alvaro Barreal provided a clinical pass to Neymar , who made no mistake in finding the target. This opening goal gave the home side a deserved lead, reflecting their offensive pressure during the first half . Tactical Shifts and Second Half Drama At the start of the second half , Chapecoense looked like a different team following a triple substitution. The tactical gamble paid off almost immediately in the 52nd minute; Giovanni Augusto found Marcinho , who clinicaly finished to bring the scores level. However, the momentum shifted back to Santos in the 62nd minute through an unfortunate own goal by Joao Ananias , putting the hosts back in front. As the clock ticked down, the match became increasingly physical. A flurry of yellow cards followed, with Lucas Verissimo , Matheus Aurelio , and Neymar all being booked as the intensity reached boiling point. Each player fought for every inch of grass, leading to a fragmented but thrilling final twenty minutes. Clinical Finish from the Penalty Spot The defining moment of the match arrived in the 89th minute. After Bruno Matias was cautioned for a foul in the box, Santos were awarded a penalty. Neymar stepped up under immense pressure and calmly converted his second of the night. Despite eight minutes of stoppage time, Santos held firm to secure the victory in a sports spectacle that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the very end."
